{"title":"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number that you receive.\n</p><p>The scale shown is balanced.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(on the left side: square, square, square, triangle, triangle on the right side: square, triangle, circle)\n</p><p>Each box has a mass of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55abf8d02ea87ea314c09b933935eec650e3fba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\text{ g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, and each triangle has a mass of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0967d6890fe6aa6830a6ee18b7878c6194882e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{2} \\text{ g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"39\" />. What is the mass, in grams, of the circle?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles on the left side by counting. We also see that there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of each shape on the right.\n</p><p>This also means that the circle's mass must be the combined mass of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes because it would have to balance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c608cce944a21ceaf74b4bd20c83aab2e0b95ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 - 1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> boxes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06ab00f8e7c899cb7e33d511044d4d3df7180fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> triangles.\n</p><p>The mass of each box is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55abf8d02ea87ea314c09b933935eec650e3fba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\text{ g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and the weight of each triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4868b882badcd282e799278889d0c3c45f14f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{2} \\text { g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"39\" />. Using the fact above, that means the mass of each circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676d692df45a30b93715e9774b02aa29345813f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\times 2 + \\frac{N}{2} = \\frac{N \\times 4}{2} + \\frac{N}{2} = \\frac{5N}{2} \\text { g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 2\">player 2</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d19e8d954853628a431ba511f77bad0311ba7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the mass of each circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/13648f4f0c4170667b1ec9c9890b1841fc2c3d57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5 \\times 24}{2} = 5 \\times 12 = \\boxed{60 \\text{ g}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC\">2024 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 2\">Relay A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 4\">Relay A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a hr